{"text": "10017-5592\n\nTo: All Employees Date: June 20, 1994\n\nFrom: Bill Murray and Geoff Bible\n\n\u2018Yesterday, the company announced that Mike Miles decided to resign. The Philip Morris\nBoard of Directors accepted Mike\u2019s resignation and appointed Bill Murray Chairman and\nGeoff Bible President and Chief Executive Officer.\n\n\u2018We want to share with you our views about these changes and our enthusiasm for the future of\nthe company. First, we ask you all to join us in wishing Mike Miles the best of luck in the\nfuture. Mike joined the Philip Morris family in 1988. Since that time, Mike has played an\ninstrumental role in bringing us together as an organization. Ie successfully joined Philip\nMorris\u2019 existing food businesses with Kraft, forming Kraft General Foods. We are proud of\nKGF's growth. Indeed, itis now the second largest food company in the world, More than\nthat, we are proud of the people that make up the KGF businesses around the world. Mike also\nplayed a major role in developing our domestic tobacco strategy. As the results come in, the\nimportance of that contribution is being appreciated even by those who questioned our pricing\n\nactions last year.\n\nItis now time to look forward, and we see a future that will be very rewarding. We are\ncentering a period in which we have never been as well positioned around the world in all three\nlines of our business -- food, tobacco and beer.\n\u2018You know both of us well and know that we are absolutely dedicated to growing all of our\nbusinesses. We are in very good shape now as we approach the mid-point of 1994, and we\nshould see good profit growth for the remainder of the year and beyond.\nur optimism for the business is based on three key strengths which are:\n\n+ our remarkable portfolio of the world\u2019s finest brands;\n\n+ a well developed global organization which is unmatched by any of our competitors,\n\nLeedzgezoz", "words": [{"text": "10017-5592", "x0": 81, "y0": 147, "x1"